      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Note: ch 3 counts as first tr throughout."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 2 tr into ring. Ch 2. *(3 tr, ch 2)*; repeat 3 more times. Pull tail to close. Join with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "slip-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "sl st"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to top of ch 3. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to corner sp. Ch 3. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into corner sp (standard granny corner). Ch 3. Sl st into the top of the next cluster of round 1*; repeat from * to * 3 more times, ending with (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in last corner, ch 3, sl st to top of ch 3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 4 ch-3 arches.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to corner sp. Ch 3. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into corner sp. Into each ch-3 arch on this side: work 3 "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "double-crochet-uk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "*; repeat from * to * around, ending with sl st to top of ch 3. (36 tr, 12 dc, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to corner sp. Ch 3. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into corner sp. For each 3-dc cluster along the side: ch 3, sl st into the top of the cluster*; repeat from * to * around, ending with sl st to top of ch 3. Fasten off. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 12 ch-3 arches.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "slug": "crochet-motif-lace-square"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in tails. Wet-block by pinning the four corners to 90 degrees and opening each chain arch with a pin through the centre of the loop. The arch count per side is three, so three pins per side plus four corner pins gives sixteen pins total for a fully squared and opened motif."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join lace squares at the corner ch-2 spaces or link the outer arches of adjacent motifs with a ch-1 join worked in the final round. The open arch structure also accepts a joining strip worked between motifs in a contrasting colour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash in cool water. Block again after washing; the chain arches collapse without pinning."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The lacy circle motif uses the same chain-arch technique around a circle rather than a square. The sunburst square adds a spiked centre structure but returns to solid granny construction from round 3 onward."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
